  (text "POWER IS OFF THE SHELF: an old ATX tower supply's main plug in J9 (Rico, 2026-10-28).\nA 20-pin plug seats in this 24-pin header; pins 11, 12, 23, 24 stay empty.\n+5V enters through F1 (3A slow-blow, 5x20): an ATX 5V rail delivers 20-30A into a fault.\nC91/C92 are the bulk at the entry: place them at F1's output.\nRails drawn are what the unit delivers: +5V, +3.3V, +12V, -12V, GND. No -5V is drawn.\n-12V is low current on any unit: every card states its +/-12V draw on its root page.\nPS_ON#: the unit runs while J10 is shorted. Panel switch or jumper.\n+5VSB and PWR_OK: real pins, nothing consumes them."
    (at 25.4 40.64 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "cae92ae9-d965-405c-8fa2-5c3a3fed4a02")
  )
